          "login": "dtolnay"
        },
        "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
        "body": "I misinterpreted \"without doing any processing\" in your proposal - I was thinking processing as in performing UTF-8 validation. Without interpreting escape sequences, this is a breaking change because the string containing backslash+n used to deserialize as one byte and now it deserializes as two bytes. Would this still be useful to you if we interpret escape sequences but just don't do the final from_utf8 conversion?",
